{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0EW4", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$K|_{X'}$", "MATH_0002": "$b_{small}^{-1}K$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0004": "$K$", "MATH_0005": "$i_*(\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet|_Z)$", "MATH_0006": "$Ri_*(K|_Z)$", "MATH_0007": "$i_*$", "MATH_0008": "$b_{small}^{-1}\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet \\to \\mathcal{I}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{I}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0010": "$X'_\\etale$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet \\to b_*(\\mathcal{I}^\\bullet)$", "MATH_0012": "$b_*(\\mathcal{I}^\\bullet)$", "MATH_0013": "$Rb_*(K|_{X'})$", "MATH_0014": "$\\pi_*(\\mathcal{I}^\\bullet|_E) = (b_*\\mathcal{I}^\\bullet)|_Z$", "MATH_0015": "$R\\pi_*(K|_E)$", "MATH_0016": "$$\nRi_*(K|_Z) \\oplus Rb_*(K|_{X'}) \\to Rc_*(K|_E)\n$$", "MATH_0017": "$$\ni_*(\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet|_Z) \\oplus\nb_*(\\mathcal{I}^\\bullet)\n\\to\ni_*\\left(b_*(\\mathcal{I}^\\bullet)|_Z\\right)\n$$", "MATH_0018": "$\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet \\to i_*(\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet|_Z) \\oplus\nb_*(\\mathcal{I}^\\bullet)$", "MATH_0019": "$\\overline{x}$", "MATH_0020": "$X$", "MATH_0021": "$\\overline{x}$", "MATH_0022": "$Z$", "MATH_0023": "$X' \\to X$", "MATH_0024": "$\\overline{x}$", "MATH_0025": "$\\overline{x}'$", "MATH_0026": "$X'$", "MATH_0027": "$$\n\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet_{\\overline{x}} \\to \\mathcal{I}^\\bullet_{\\overline{x}'}\n$$", "MATH_0028": "$\\mathcal{I}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0029": "$\\overline{x}$", "MATH_0030": "$Z$", "MATH_0031": "$b_(\\mathcal{I}^\\bullet)_{\\overline{x}} \\to \ni_*\\left(b_*(\\mathcal{I}^\\bullet)|_Z\\right)_{\\overline{x}}$", "MATH_0032": "$i_*(\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet|_Z)_{\\overline{x}} =\n\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet_{\\overline{x}}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{proposition-finite-higher-direct-image-zero}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-proper-base-change-f-star}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-proper-base-change}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{derived-section-canonical-delta-functor}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0cbeea7c3db6e349f4244998419cc7413e9353507b65ae65f84c5e94ae157571", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2943c72a05e6627cf9fbaa4cc89c8374b9c074e32076a40e03efdb9ab6d583fb", "source_text": "The notation <MATH_0001> stands for <MATH_0002>.\nChoose a bounded below complex <MATH_0003>\nof abelian sheaves representing <MATH_0004>. Observe that\n<MATH_0005> represents <MATH_0006>\nbecause <MATH_0007> is exact\n(Proposition <REF_0001>).\nChoose a quasi-isomorphism\n<MATH_0008>\nwhere <MATH_0009> is a bounded below complex of injective\nabelian sheaves on <MATH_0010>. This map is adjoint to a map\n<MATH_0011> and\n<MATH_0012> represents <MATH_0013>.\nWe have <MATH_0014>\nby Lemma <REF_0002> and by\nLemma <REF_0003> this complex represents\n<MATH_0015>. Hence the map\n<MATH_0016>\nis represented by the surjective map of bounded below complexes\n<MATH_0017>\nTo get our distinguished triangle it suffices to show that\nthe canonical map\n<MATH_0018>\nmaps quasi-isomorphically onto the kernel of the map\nof complexes displayed above (namely a short exact sequence\nof complexes determines a distinguished triangle in the derived\ncategory, see\nDerived Categories, Section <REF_0004>).\nWe may check this on stalks at a geometric point <MATH_0019> of <MATH_0020>.\nIf <MATH_0021> is not in <MATH_0022>, then <MATH_0023> is an isomorphism\nover an open neighbourhood of <MATH_0024>. Thus, if <MATH_0025>\ndenotes the corresponding geometric point of <MATH_0026> in this case, then\nwe have to show that\n<MATH_0027>\nis a quasi-isomorphism. This is true by our choice of <MATH_0028>.\nIf <MATH_0029> is in <MATH_0030>, then\n<MATH_0031>\nis an isomorphism of complexes of abelian groups. Hence the\nkernel is equal to\n<MATH_0032> as desired.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:23a4ff2968119be1ea9738377bfb5f2dfc3b7ad89c4cb4a848c17676618dc322", "unit_id": "tag:0EW5:proof"}
